.TH SYSGLANCE 1 "2026-11-05" "sysglance 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sysglance \- show system information at a glance, quickly
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysglance
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysglance
prints information about the running Linux system (distribution, kernel,
CPU, GPU, memory, disks, packages and more) next to an ASCII logo.
All information is read directly from
.IR /proc ,
.IR /sys ,
.I /etc/os-release
and a few system calls; no external programs are executed.
A typical run takes well under five milliseconds.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-modules " " \fILIST\fR
Comma separated list of modules to show, in order.
Duplicates are allowed. See
.BR \-\-list\-modules .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list\-modules
List available modules with a short description and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-logos
List available logos and the distribution ids they are used for.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print machine readable JSON instead of the logo and text.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Force colored output, even if standard output is not a terminal and
.B NO_COLOR
is set.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-logo
Do not print the logo.
.TP
.BI \-\-logo " NAME"
Use the named logo instead of auto-detecting one.
.B none
disables the logo.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Read configuration from
.IR FILE .
It is an error if the file cannot be read.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Do not read the default configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " DIR"
Read every system file below
.I DIR
instead of
.IR / .
Intended for testing against fixture trees.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.PP
Options taking a value also accept the
.BI \-\-option= value
form.
.SH MODULES
title, os, host, kernel, uptime, packages, shell, terminal, cpu, gpu, memory,
swap, disk, localip, battery, loadavg, processes, locale, user, hostname.
Modules whose data is unavailable (for example
.B battery
on a desktop) are silently omitted from text output and reported with
.B \(dqavailable\(dq: false
in JSON output.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default configuration file is
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sysglance/config.ini
or
.I ~/.config/sysglance/config.ini
if
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset. It is optional. Command line options override it.
.PP
.nf
# comments start with # or ;
[display]
color = auto          # auto | true | false
logo = true
logo_name = auto      # auto | none | a name from \-\-list\-logos
separator = ": "      # quotes keep leading/trailing spaces
key_color = auto      # auto | red | bright\-blue | ...
json = false

[modules]
list = title, os, kernel, cpu, memory
.fi
.PP
Unknown sections, keys or values are reported with their line number and
make sysglance exit with status 1.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to a non-empty value, colors are disabled unless
.B \-\-color
is given.
.TP
.B SYSGLANCE_ROOT
Same as
.BR \-\-root .
.TP
.BR USER ", " SHELL ", " TERM ", " TERM_PROGRAM ", " LC_ALL ", " LANG
Used by the user, shell, terminal and locale modules.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error or write error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line usage (unknown option, module or logo).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sysglance
sysglance \-\-modules os,kernel,memory \-\-no\-logo
sysglance \-\-json | python3 \-m json.tool
NO_COLOR=1 sysglance > info.txt
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uname (1),
.BR free (1),
.BR df (1),
.BR proc (5),
.BR os-release (5)
